---- MODULE MCParReach ----
EXTENDS Integers, Sequences, FiniteSets

CONSTANTS Nodes, Root, Procs, Succ

VARIABLES marked, frontier, pc, sel, succ

Vars == <<marked, frontier, pc, sel, succ>>

\* Succ is reinterpreted by a substitution in the .cfg that injects the
\* specific graph structure; the declaration here is just its shape.
Types == /\ marked \subseteq Nodes
         /\ frontier \subseteq Nodes
         /\ pc \in [Procs -> {"idle", "hasNode"}]
         /\ sel \in [Procs -> Nodes \cup {"none"}]
         /\ succ \in [Nodes -> SUBSET Nodes]

Init == /\ marked = {}
        /\ frontier = {Root}
        /\ pc = [p \in Procs |-> "idle"]
        /\ sel = [p \in Procs |-> "none"]
        /\ succ = [n \in Nodes |-> {}]

\* Pick a frontier node and compute its successors in the same step.
Pick(p, n) == /\ pc[p] = "idle"
              /\ n \in frontier
              /\ frontier' = frontier \ {n}
              /\ pc' = [pc EXCEPT ![p] = "hasNode"]
              /\ sel' = [sel EXCEPT ![p] = n]
              /\ succ' = [succ EXCEPT ![n] = Succ[n]]
              /\ UNCHANGED marked

Mark(p) == /\ pc[p] = "hasNode"
           /\ sel[p] \notin marked
           /\ marked' = marked \cup {sel[p]}
           /\ frontier' = frontier \cup succ[sel[p]]
           /\ pc' = [pc EXCEPT ![p] = "idle"]
           /\ sel' = [sel EXCEPT ![p] = "none"]
           /\ UNCHANGED succ

Abandon(p) == /\ pc[p] = "hasNode"
              /\ sel[p] \in marked
              /\ pc' = [pc EXCEPT ![p] = "idle"]
              /\ sel' = [sel EXCEPT ![p] = "none"]
              /\ UNCHANGED <<marked, frontier, succ>>

Idle == \A p \in Procs : pc[p] = "idle" /\ frontier = {} /\ UNCHANGED Vars

Next == Idle \/ (\E p \in Procs, n \in Nodes : Pick(p, n)) \/ (\E p \in Procs : Mark(p) \/ Abandon(p))

Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_Vars

\* The inductive invariant combines type correctness with reachability
\* control flow: a node is marked exactly when it is outside the frontier
\* and it is in frontier exactly while unmarked. Together these force a
\* node to be marked before it can be picked up as a frontier node.
Inv == /\ \A n \in Nodes : n \in marked => n \notin frontier
       /\ \A n \in Nodes : n \in frontier => n \notin marked
       /\ Types

\* The reachable subgraph is exactly the subgraph generated by the
\* currently marked nodes, which is the sequential algorithm's result.
Refines == frontier = {n \in Nodes : \E m \in marked : n \in Succ[m]}

LimitedSeq == Seq

====